From 0e4b5bed472abcd4c4b1eeadf2dc99ae7f8651dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:59:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The Barrows, fixed from play: four things that could not work

Corey played it and found four. Three of them share one root cause and it is worth writing down.

A HANDLER ON A MULTILOC CHILD NEVER FIRES. A multiloc has a shell on the map and children it
resolves to, and the ops the player sees come from the child - so a trigger written on the child
looks right, reads right and compiles. Player.getOpTrigger looks the script up on
LocType.get(target.type), the type that is ON THE MAP, and does not resolve the multiloc, even
though OpLocHandler resolved one moments earlier to decide whether the op exists at all. So
[oploc1,barrows_door_unlocked_l], [oploc1,barrows_ladder] and [oploc1,barrows_stone_chest_closed]
were three scripts that could not run: no door in the tunnels opened, no ladder climbed, and the
chest could not be opened at all. The thirty-two door shells and the four ladder shells carry
category=barrows_door / category=barrows_ladder now - the shape open_and_close_double_doors.rs2
already uses - and the chest's one op1 handler branches on the same bit its multiloc reads.

Every check that existed asked whether the trigger was WRITTEN DOWN. The battery now asks whether
it can run: every [oploc*] the Barrows declares must name a loc that is on one of the two Barrows
maps, or a category such a loc carries, AND that loc must really have that op, on itself or on a
multiloc child. The reverse too - no Barrows loc on either map has an option nothing handles.

THE DIG WOULD NOT STOP. human_dig_long is loops=8, so it outlives the two ticks the script waits
and the telejump does not end it: the player arrived in the crypt still shovelling until they
clicked something else. anim(null, 0) after the jump, the way quest_zombiequeen.rs2 ends its own
long dig.

NOTHING IN THE TUNNELS DROPS ANYTHING NOW. The two Barrows skeletons were on the ordinary skeleton
table - coins, arrows, runes, a herb and a shot at the ultra-rare - in a place whose entire reward
is the chest at the end of it. They are off it. And death_drop DEFAULTS TO BONES, so the crypt rat
and the giant crypt rat were quietly dropping bones through [ai_queue3,_] -> ~npc_default_death:
all seven tunnel monsters say param=death_drop,null out loud, which is the only way to drop
nothing.

Two more found while checking those, both the same kind of fault. Searching the sarcophagus of a
brother who was already up and still alive added a SECOND copy of him, because the kill bit only
says he is dead - the boxes ask ~barrows_brother_here now, the way the chest already did. And that
proc was passing HuntVis 1 (LINEOFSIGHT) where it needed 0 (OFF), so a brother two rooms away
answered "not here" and the chest would have handed out a second one.

Verified: clean build, rs2check 1699 scripts / 490 configs with 0 ERROR and 0 CHECK, all eleven
batteries green, and barrows_battery.py's 523 checks against 120 mutations - each caught by its own
check. The ninth "a crash is not a catch" turned up on the way: the new dig check used .rindex on a
string that the mutation removes, which raises instead of failing.

